+
+The argument's chain is:
+
+1. Use the zero-framed Chebyshev irreducible colors C_r and multiplicativity C_r(K#J)=C_r(K)C_r(J)/S_r(delta). The source is Morton–Strickland Theorem 1.1 / Corollary 1.2 and Theorem 2.1. Check the empty=1 normalization and the framing.
+2. Prove the universal kernel has the necessary delta-adic filtration, coefficientwise in every E_k(J). The all-n proof uses reflection polynomials P_s(r)=binom((r+s)/2,s), not a numerical limit. Check the ODD-r reciprocal and the claimed cancellation degree especially carefully.
+3. Apply Casson's stable-ribbon fact: smooth slice K admits ribbon J with K#J ribbon. The filtered diagonal is 1 or d(J), so full parallel divisibility descends to K by induction.
+4. Extract leading connected-sum laws: F_(K#J)=F_K F_J/cos x and G_(K#J)=G_K G_J/(sin x/x), for the defined even and odd exponential series. Check the factorials and signs. Prove coefficients are in Z_(2) BEFORE any mod-32 reduction. The odd case uses a reciprocal recurrence with odd pivot and a binary-digit factorial valuation.
+5. Use those triangular laws and d(K),d(J)=1 mod8 to transfer e_n=d^n mod32 for every n.
+6. For any finite annular skein support, evaluate P on S_p=#^p 6_1. The even e_(2a)(S_p) and odd e_(2a+1)(S_p)/9^p are degree-a polynomials in p, with nonzero leading coefficients controlled by e2(6_1)-1=48 and e3(6_1)-9=1776. A Vandermonde forces v_delta(a_j)>=max(0,m-j). This matrix is inverted over Q at the root, NOT modulo32; Gauss then restores integral divisibility.
